<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03ZU">Remark <span data-tag="03ZU">8.5.3.2</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a category. It follows from Remark <a data-tag="03ZP" href="/tag/03ZP">8.5.2.8</a> (and Proposition <a data-tag="002Z" href="/tag/002Z">1.3.3.1</a>) that evaluation on the morphism $\widetilde{e} \in \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Idem}}( \widetilde{X}, \widetilde{X})$ supplies a bijection from the set of idempotents in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03ZT" href="/tag/03ZT">8.5.3.1</a>) to the set of idempotent endomorphisms $(X,e)$ in the category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="03ZF" href="/tag/03ZF">8.5.2.1</a>). We can therefore view Definition <a data-tag="03ZT" href="/tag/03ZT">8.5.3.1</a> as a generalization of Definition <a data-tag="03ZF" href="/tag/03ZF">8.5.2.1</a>. </p>
